For example, given the list [1, -2, 3, -4, 5, -6], the maximum subarray sum is 15, which is the sum of the first 4 numbers in the list.
In C++ and Java, find maximum subarray sum can be done by using dynamic programming.

C++:
int maxSubarraySum(int arr[], int n) {
  if (n == 1) {
    return arr[0];
  }
  int max = arr[0];
  for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    int curr_max = max;
    for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      curr_max = max;
      curr_max = max + arr[i];
      max = max > curr_max? max : curr_max;
    }
  }
  return max;
}

